CiukiOS f6-20: the layout time limit applies to remote content only; a
rejection never ends the browser. layout_document/textplain_reformat classify
the content URL (about:, resource: and file: are local: structural admission
only; every other scheme also gets the 75 ms limit, nested spans inherit an
outer deadline). Rejections log class, cause and elapsed time and show the
error page; after an error on the current content (rejection after READY) the
page's parameters return to loading_parameters so the error page's Try Again
re-fetches it. The frontend records why its main loop ended and prints one
"[netsurf] exit reason=..." line before netsurf_exit's lwc leak report.
Evidence: docs/validation/2026-10-22-f6-20-netsurf-budget-exit.md (host
tests/host/netsurf); the port files add the channel drain and keepalive.

